Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.00,0:00:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,THIS EPISODE HAS SELF-HARM.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.33,0:00:09.04,Default,,0,0,0,,FOR HELP,\NWWW.WANNATALKABOUTIT.COM.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.58,0:00:54.71,Default,,0,0,0,,MAGISTRATE
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.50,0:00:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,What gives you the right?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.54,0:01:03.87,Default,,0,0,0,,What gives you the right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.50,0:01:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Pleasure, sir. I'm Apolinar Moscote…
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.33,0:01:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,and I was named magistrate of this town.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.29,0:01:17.92,Default,,0,0,0,,No pieces of paper rules over our people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.83,0:01:20.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And by the way,\Nwe don't need any magistrate,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.00,0:01:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,because there's nothing here to fix!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.71,0:01:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I should warn you, I am armed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.04,0:01:59.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I would rather carry you alive
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.50,0:02:03.21,Default,,0,0,0,,than carry your death\Nwith me for the rest of my life.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.25,0:02:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,,ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.13,0:02:51.26,Default,,0,0,0,,When Úrsula arranged\Nfor the expansion of the house,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.96,0:02:54.46,Default,,0,0,0,,she had a special room built\Nfor Melquiades
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.33,0:02:59.50,Default,,0,0,0,,where he would spend hours on end\Nscribbling his enigmatic literature.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.08,0:03:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Arcadio…
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.75,0:03:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Years later,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.33,0:03:11.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Arcadio would remember trembling
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.21,0:03:15.25,Default,,0,0,0,,as Melquiades made him listen\Nto pages of his impenetrable writing.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.71,0:03:19.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Writings which,\Nalthough he couldn't understand,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.75,0:03:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,were actually predicting his death.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.33,0:04:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,QUIET STREET
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.96,0:04:49.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The image of Remedios\Nached somewhere inside Aureliano's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.71,0:04:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It was a physical sensation
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.33,0:04:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,that almost made it difficult\Nfor him to walk,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.42,0:04:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,like a pebble in his shoe.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.88,0:05:02.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Move!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.33,0:05:22.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, we already tried to be polite.\NHe's gonna have to learn the hard way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.54,0:05:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,My friend, you know\NI'm at your complete disposal.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.00,0:05:27.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My boy and I will always stand by you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.13,0:05:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,We all stand with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.42,0:05:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.38,0:05:31.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He brought company.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.71,0:05:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,We know he brought\Nsome armed soldiers with him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.04,0:05:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,He also brought his wife and daughters.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.21,0:05:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Moscote!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.71,0:05:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Show your face out here now!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.54,0:05:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it, Buendía?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.71,0:05:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen closely.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.42,0:05:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Nearly 30 years ago,\Nthese men and I started building Macondo.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.21,0:06:01.71,Default,,0,0,0,,We created roads, marked every street,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.79,0:06:03.37,Default,,0,0,0,,even built every house,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.29,0:06:06.75,Default,,0,0,0,,all of which was done\Nwithout the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.75,0:06:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,And we want things to stay that way.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.33,0:06:14.58,Default,,0,0,0,,But you're welcome to live with us\Nif that's what you really want.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.75,0:06:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,And not because you have\Na bunch of gunmen here protecting you,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.71,0:06:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,but out of courtesy and consideration\Nfor your missus and daughters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.71,0:06:32.67,Default,,0,0,0,,However, there are two conditions.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.71,0:06:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone can paint their house\Nthe way they see fit,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.04,0:06:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,and your little soldiers\Nare leaving today.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.00,0:06:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,And who will be enforcing law and order?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.96,0:06:47.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, us.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.88,0:06:51.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you believe Macondo's so peaceful
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.71,0:06:54.29,Default,,0,0,0,,that its first person\Nhas not even died from natural causes?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.38,0:06:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Much less unnatural.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.88,0:06:58.51,Default,,0,0,0,,We don't even have a cemetery.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.96,0:07:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Your word of honor?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.92,0:07:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Word of your enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.38,0:07:07.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Because you and I are still enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.88,0:07:17.55,Default,,0,0,0,,FOUNDED IN 1880
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.42,0:07:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Amparo, grab an onion.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.25,0:07:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.21,0:08:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,That one is rotten.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.79,0:08:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Moscote…\NI am Úrsula Iguarán de Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.75,0:08:11.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I see your husband mentioned mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.13,0:08:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,They may have got off on the wrong foot,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.25,0:08:18.96,Default,,0,0,0,,but there's no purpose in you and I\Ndoing the same as far as I'm concerned.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.38,0:08:24.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Úrsula, I've heard your house is\Nthe most exquisite of them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.58,0:08:26.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, my doors\Nare always open to your family.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.75,0:08:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Come visit us anytime.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.25,0:08:29.63,Default,,0,0,0,,-Thank you.\N-Mm-hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.71,0:08:32.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Wonderful to meet you, Mrs. Úrsula.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.38,0:08:34.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Likewise, Mrs. Moscote.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.46,0:08:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,-That's all right.\N-I'll pay.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.54,0:08:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-No need, ma'am. My gift.\N-Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.63,0:09:05.01,Default,,0,0,0,,If he sees me using the daguerreotype,\Nthen I won't hear the end of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.08,0:09:08.79,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. So you tell him\Nthat since he's forgotten it exists,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.38,0:09:11.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I gave it to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.33,0:09:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I have achieved immortality.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.83,0:09:40.66,Default,,0,0,0,,THE CHOLERA
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.75,0:09:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,"You have to succumb\Nto the sophisticated talk
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.92,0:09:46.96,Default,,0,0,0,,of the most inept in a secretarial class\Nin addition to…"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.54,0:09:51.08,Default,,0,0,0,,-Please come in.\N-Thank you for having us.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.04,0:09:54.58,Default,,0,0,0,,We've brought you a gift.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.67,0:09:55.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.04,0:09:57.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Made by my daughters.\N-Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.50,0:09:59.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You should see the tablecloths.\NThey're divine.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.96,0:10:02.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I can imagine. Visitación!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.42,0:10:05.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Could you please bring\Nshortbread and biscuits to the ladies?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.00,0:10:06.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.96,0:10:11.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Moscote and her daughters.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.54,0:10:21.12,Default,,0,0,0,,-This is the living room.\N-It's beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.21,0:10:24.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm. We have put\Na lot of work into the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.08,0:10:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-I'm sure.\N-Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.79,0:10:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-It can be quite a lot to maintain.\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.71,0:10:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,These are my daughters,\NAmaranta and Rebeca.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.79,0:10:34.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-Pleasure.\N-Nice to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.00,0:10:37.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's show Mrs. Leonor\Nand her daughters around.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.17,0:10:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,-Welcome.\N-This way.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.46,0:10:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.46,0:10:41.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, a pianola!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.00,0:10:43.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but it's out of tune.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.96,0:10:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you coming?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.04,0:10:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You really do have\Na beautiful home.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.04,0:10:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.88,0:11:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-This is the Corridor of Begonias.\N-Mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.50,0:11:13.29,Default,,0,0,0,,The girls' rooms are over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.33,0:11:17.54,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's the kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.08,0:11:21.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Please enjoy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.42,0:11:24.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.04,0:11:36.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Our granary is over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.92,0:11:40.88,Default,,0,0,0,,How pretty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.38,0:11:42.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Did you make this?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.92,0:11:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-And here…\N-Do you like it?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.63,0:11:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's José Arcadio's laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.29,0:11:54.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.83,0:11:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You can have it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.29,0:12:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios, get out of there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.17,0:12:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.54,0:12:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,That afternoon,\NAureliano lost the hidden patience
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.58,0:12:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,that had made him wait\Nfor a chance to see her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.79,0:12:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And the house suddenly filled with love.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.00,0:12:39.00,Default,,0,0,0,,My darling Rebeca,\NI think about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.42,0:12:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I dream about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.92,0:12:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios in the soporific air\Nof 2:00 in the afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.54,0:12:59.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios in the soft breathing of roses.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.42,0:13:03.05,Default,,0,0,0,,My beloved Pietro,\Nthe days feel different now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.13,0:13:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I cannot wait to be back in Macondo.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.88,0:13:08.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios, everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.17,0:13:11.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios, forever for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.96,0:13:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios… everywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.58,0:13:48.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It has been days\Nsince your last letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.38,0:13:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Will I see you again?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.08,0:13:55.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Amparo!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.67,0:13:58.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The postman hasn't come.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.79,0:14:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,♪ Oye, morenita, ven, dame tu amor… ♪
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.58,0:14:51.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey! The world is spinning!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.71,0:14:53.63,Default,,0,0,0,,♪ De mi corazón ♪
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.13,0:15:00.09,Default,,0,0,0,,♪ Oye, morenita, no quiero perderte ♪
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.17,0:15:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,♪ Y si tú me dejas, prefiero la muerte… ♪
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.67,0:15:23.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano, tell us.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.88,0:15:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is the woman that's got you like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.29,0:15:28.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Like this how?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.25,0:15:30.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Like screwed.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.67,0:15:41.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano! It's eleven o'clock almost!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.96,0:15:53.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano then lost his memory,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.96,0:15:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,just like during the times of oblivion.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.25,0:16:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,And he recovered it on a strange dawn
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.04,0:16:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,in a room completely unfamiliar to him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.17,0:16:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,He didn't know how he had gotten there,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.75,0:16:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,but he knew what his purpose was…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.29,0:16:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,because he had carried it\Nhidden since childhood
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.38,0:16:26.96,Default,,0,0,0,,in an impenetrable pocket in his heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.88,0:17:13.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.00,0:17:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to get it off your chest.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.38,0:17:23.26,Default,,0,0,0,,All of this anguish is killing you,\Nand I'm dying to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.00,0:17:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios Moscote.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.29,0:17:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, first, you're gonna\Nhave to convince your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.58,0:17:52.29,Default,,0,0,0,,And after that, her father.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.08,0:18:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Beneath her mockery,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.75,0:18:05.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano found a haven of understanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.08,0:18:11.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That dawn, he not only let go\Nof his doubts about his virility,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.67,0:18:15.59,Default,,0,0,0,,but also, the bitter weight\Nhe had carried in his heart
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.67,0:18:17.21,Default,,0,0,0,,for so many months.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.08,0:18:29.33,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.67,0:18:33.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Your sister's eating dirt again.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.63,0:19:02.76,Default,,0,0,0,,"My darling…"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.08,0:19:10.37,Default,,0,0,0,,"I love you"?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.46,0:19:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I love you too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.75,0:19:22.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.63,0:19:30.80,Default,,0,0,0,,What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.42,0:19:35.17,Default,,0,0,0,,How did all these letters get here?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.13,0:19:49.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Here's the water.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.96,0:19:54.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.75,0:19:59.92,Default,,0,0,0,,They're from the Italian.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.88,0:20:04.88,Default,,0,0,0,,"My beloved Rebeca,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.67,0:20:09.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know when I come or when I go,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.75,0:20:12.42,Default,,0,0,0,,nor if all this is real or just a dream."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.88,0:20:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,"Every decision I make contradicts\Nthe decision that I made before it."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.75,0:20:21.88,Default,,0,0,0,,"And through all the things\Nthat my soul conceives,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:21.96,0:20:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I have decided to go to Macondo\Nto ask for your hand in marriage."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.04,0:20:26.71,Default,,0,0,0,,"For your hand."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.13,0:20:30.46,Default,,0,0,0,,"I will let you know\Nthe date of my arrival
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.54,0:20:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,in the next letter."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.67,0:21:02.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta also suffered\Nfrom the thorn of a lonely love.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.50,0:21:04.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta, open up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.21,0:21:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,She would lock herself\Nin the bathroom,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.58,0:21:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,to find release\Nfrom the torment of a hopeless passion.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.67,0:21:22.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.42,0:21:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta, open the door.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.00,0:21:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,So he was also writing to Amaranta?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.96,0:21:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.83,0:21:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,She wrote him letters
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.25,0:21:55.33,Default,,0,0,0,,and never sent them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.21,0:22:00.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish I had never thought\Nabout buying that pianola.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:19.13,0:22:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,One more.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.92,0:22:25.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Another one.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.63,0:22:30.59,Default,,0,0,0,,That's how many?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.58,0:22:32.46,Default,,0,0,0,,More than ten.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:33.83,0:22:34.87,Default,,0,0,0,,There he is.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.00,0:22:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Moscote!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.83,0:22:45.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:48.58,0:22:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought we made a deal.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:50.29,0:22:51.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I've honored it.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:52.17,0:22:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought we both agreed no one\Nwould have to paint their house blue.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.00,0:22:55.83,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.38,0:22:57.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You were very clear about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.04,0:23:00.54,Default,,0,0,0,,"Everyone can paint their house\Nthe way they see fit."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.13,0:23:02.17,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what they're doing.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.25,0:23:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You're telling me\Nyou have nothing to do with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.04,0:23:07.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The government gives away the paint.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.08,0:23:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I deliver it.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.71,0:23:10.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't force anybody.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.04,0:23:12.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Good day, gentlemen.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:17.79,0:23:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,How unlucky can you get?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.92,0:23:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.29,0:23:23.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Moscote.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.54,0:23:26.62,Default,,0,0,0,,He thinks he can just mock us.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.17,0:23:33.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no. What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.63,0:23:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.29,0:23:41.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I've fallen in love.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.83,0:23:46.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you also in love with Crespi?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.17,0:23:47.13,Default,,0,0,0,,No, of course not.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:53.29,0:23:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, Remedios Moscote.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.21,0:24:06.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You fell in love with\Nthe daughter of my enemy, son?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:09.79,0:24:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Love is an awful plague.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:14.25,0:24:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Come here.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.83,0:24:16.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Come.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.17,0:24:24.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Does she love you back, son?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:25.63,0:24:26.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.21,0:24:28.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't said anything to her yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:29.00,0:24:31.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, then, forget about this little whim.\NMove on, son.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.50,0:24:33.96,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not just a whim.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:34.54,0:24:37.12,Default,,0,0,0,,I really am in love with her,\Nand I'd like to marry her.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:37.21,0:24:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The Moscotes are\Nfine young women, José Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.79,0:24:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Your problem is her father, not the girl.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.88,0:24:44.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Apolinar Moscote\Nwill never be a part of this family.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:51.38,0:24:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Our family exists
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.75,0:24:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,because you and Mother had\Nthe courage to confront your own parents.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.92,0:25:00.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't even think of comparing
Dialogue: 0,0:25:01.21,0:25:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,your grandparents'\Nridiculous superstitions
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.79,0:25:08.37,Default,,0,0,0,,to the menace Apolinar Moscote is\Nto Macondo, for God's sake!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:13.13,0:25:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll ask for Remedios's hand in marriage…
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.79,0:25:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,with or without your blessing, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.00,0:25:25.33,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía…
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.17,0:25:29.42,Default,,0,0,0,,you've lost one son.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.92,0:25:32.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you willing to lose another?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.88,0:25:45.80,Default,,0,0,0,,If we're marrying Aureliano off\Nto the daughter of Moscote,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.79,0:25:49.37,Default,,0,0,0,,then we will let\NRebeca marry Pietro Crespi.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.46,0:26:05.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebeca regained her health
Dialogue: 0,0:26:06.04,0:26:08.17,Default,,0,0,0,,as soon as she heard\Nabout the arrangement.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:09.79,0:26:11.87,Default,,0,0,0,,And she wrote her fiancé a joyful letter
Dialogue: 0,0:26:11.96,0:26:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,that she gave to her parents\Nfor their approval.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.96,0:26:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta pretended to accept the decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:43.17,0:27:46.30,Default,,0,0,0,,So, Aureliano, which of my daughters\Ndid you want to wed?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:52.13,0:27:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,W… w… well, Remedios.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:58.25,0:27:59.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you mean Amparo?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:01.88,0:28:02.76,Default,,0,0,0,,No, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.79,0:28:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Remedios.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:07.08,0:28:10.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Dolores, please bring\Nyour sister Remedios.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.38,0:28:19.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.33,0:28:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I have six daughters old enough to marry,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.42,0:28:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,and your son, specifically, likes\Nthe one who still plays with dolls.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.67,0:28:26.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:28.83,0:28:29.87,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.63,0:28:32.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:35.17,0:28:36.05,Default,,0,0,0,,All of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.83,0:28:37.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Now.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.92,0:28:43.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me handle it.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:44.17,0:28:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Buendía,\Ncould I have a moment with you… alone?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.04,0:29:02.37,Default,,0,0,0,,We had absolutely no idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:03.75,0:29:06.04,Default,,0,0,0,,-We would love to unite our two families.\N-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.13,0:29:09.34,Default,,0,0,0,,-But Remedios is still a child.\N-Well, that's pretty evident, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.92,0:29:12.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And trust me, if we knew\Nwhich daughter he was referring to,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:12.54,0:29:13.54,Default,,0,0,0,,we wouldn't be here.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.88,0:29:29.38,Default,,0,0,0,,We will let Remedios marry Aureliano,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.46,0:29:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,but… we will wait\Nuntil she's of conceiving age.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.29,0:29:36.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Under one condition.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:37.75,0:29:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:39.79,0:29:42.50,Default,,0,0,0,,They get married in a church,\Nor there's no wedding.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.04,0:29:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Macondo has always been a secular town.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:46.75,0:29:50.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I will not accept their union\Nif it isn't first blessed by the Lord.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:51.33,0:29:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,If you want is\Nfor us to marry in the church,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.54,0:29:56.67,Default,,0,0,0,,that's fine by me.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:15.13,0:30:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades,\NI need your advice.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.71,0:30:25.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Turns out that idiot of a magistrate,\Nhe intends to bring the church to Macondo.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.21,0:30:34.54,Default,,0,0,0,,When have we ever needed a priest?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.25,0:30:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:41.21,0:30:42.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:04.25,0:31:05.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Gypsy?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.88,0:31:08.96,Default,,0,0,0,,He's been like this for days.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:10.25,0:31:11.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Since when?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.17,0:31:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Since he finished his book.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.88,0:31:20.09,Default,,0,0,0,,When I die…
Dialogue: 0,0:31:23.17,0:31:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,burn mercury for three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:28.25,0:31:29.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean, my friend?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:49.71,0:31:52.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Take him to the river tomorrow\Nand let him bathe.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.17,0:31:56.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The water will do him good.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:35.50,0:32:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.75,0:32:41.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:46.33,0:32:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:50.92,0:32:51.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.83,0:32:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:06.71,0:33:07.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.71,0:33:12.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:12.25,0:33:13.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.63,0:33:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:22.83,0:33:24.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:24.42,0:33:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:29.00,0:33:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I will never forgive your negligence.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.00,0:33:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:37.83,0:33:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.96,0:33:43.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:33:46.67,0:33:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:04.04,0:34:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Hurry! Come on! Over here!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:27.21,0:34:28.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Help me take him to the laboratory.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:29.92,0:34:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,What are you waiting for?!\NLet's go! Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:58.75,0:35:02.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Buendía,\Nas the civil authority of our town,
Dialogue: 0,0:35:02.50,0:35:04.08,Default,,0,0,0,,it is my duty to inform you
Dialogue: 0,0:35:04.17,0:35:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,that a drowned man's unearthed cadaver\Npresents a major threat to public health.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.33,0:35:08.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades is not a dead man.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:10.21,0:35:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,He's immortal.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:12.79,0:35:15.37,Default,,0,0,0,,He himself revealed\Nthe formula of his resurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:26.38,0:35:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,One, two, three.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:29.75,0:35:31.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Arcadio, the furnace.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:32.21,0:35:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Mercury!
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.75,0:35:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Time has stopped,\Nand eternity has begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.38,0:36:24.76,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio…
Dialogue: 0,0:36:28.83,0:36:30.12,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio, stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.67,0:36:32.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:33.88,0:36:36.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I think that it's time\Nfor you to put him to rest now.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.79,0:37:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Time has stopped,\Nand eternity has begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:04.92,0:37:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We come from water.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:07.71,0:37:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Time has stopped and eternity has begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:32.42,0:37:33.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Time has stopped,
Dialogue: 0,0:37:34.46,0:37:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and eternity has begun, Melquiades.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:04.29,0:39:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Arcadio never knew
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.50,0:39:08.63,Default,,0,0,0,,that the woman who held him tightly,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:08.71,0:39:10.88,Default,,0,0,0,,embracing his loneliness and sorrow,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.54,0:39:12.92,Default,,0,0,0,,was really his mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:46.71,0:40:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,-Rebeca.\N-Pietro.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.13,0:40:51.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This gift is for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:54.25,0:40:57.58,Default,,0,0,0,,One, two, three.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:57.67,0:40:59.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:00.58,0:41:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The ballerina.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:11.46,0:41:12.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you like it?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:19.33,0:41:20.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Please.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.00,0:41:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,,She's angry.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:30.25,0:41:31.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait here.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:49.54,0:41:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Miss Amaranta.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.17,0:41:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:41:54.92,0:41:56.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you've been well.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.54,0:41:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted to tell you I'll be opening\Na store of musical instruments
Dialogue: 0,0:41:59.88,0:42:01.63,Default,,0,0,0,,with my brother… my brother Bruno.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:04.46,0:42:05.34,Default,,0,0,0,,So?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:06.00,0:42:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I could introduce him to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:18.04,0:42:20.08,Default,,0,0,0,,I swear you'll never marry my sister,
Dialogue: 0,0:42:21.58,0:42:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,even if you have to walk over\Nmy dead body on your way out.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:17.33,0:43:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta threatened Pietro\Nwith killing herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:23.79,0:43:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it's best\Nif we get her out of town for a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:29.33,0:43:32.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps meeting new people\Nwill help heal her disappointment.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:40.46,0:43:42.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'm worried about you.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:44.50,0:43:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't want to leave you alone right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:48.29,0:43:49.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:51.21,0:43:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:53.75,0:43:55.75,Default,,0,0,0,,The priority here is to avoid tragedy.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:57.08,0:43:58.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:16.75,0:44:17.63,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:20.00,0:44:20.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:35.88,0:44:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't get your hopes up, sis.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.25,0:44:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if I have to kill you,\NI will stop this marriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:56.92,0:44:58.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Be careful.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.13,0:45:41.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Death.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:42.92,0:45:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The card of Death?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:46.46,0:45:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The cards are never\Nto be interpreted literally.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.92,0:45:52.80,Default,,0,0,0,,So what does it mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:52.88,0:45:53.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Will I be happy?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:56.54,0:45:57.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, you will,
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.25,0:46:01.38,Default,,0,0,0,,but getting there\Nwill not be easy for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.46,0:46:06.13,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll turn you upside down\Nlike a giant whirlwind.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.08,0:46:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Rebeca.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:09.29,0:46:12.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebeca, we mustn't. No.\NRebeca, we're in your house.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.29,0:46:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Rebeca, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:14.29,0:46:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebeca, my dear.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.92,0:46:18.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:18.21,0:46:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Good afternoon, Mr. Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:21.21,0:46:22.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen Melquiades?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:26.67,0:46:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you seen Pietro's present?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.38,0:46:30.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.08,0:46:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,The rich and wondrous\Nmechanical animals Pietro Crespi brought
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.46,0:46:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,dissipated José Arcadio Buendía's\Naffliction over the death of Melquíades,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:01.21,0:47:04.25,Default,,0,0,0,,transporting him\Nto his old days as an alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:06.88,0:47:07.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Some sort of map…
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.46,0:47:10.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano, in turn,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:11.04,0:47:14.12,Default,,0,0,0,,had neglected the workshop\Nto teach young Remedios.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:17.79,0:47:21.21,Default,,0,0,0,,In my family,\NI am the only person of legal age.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:21.29,0:47:24.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Although, my eldest son\Nwill turn 21 in April.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:24.58,0:47:25.58,Default,,0,0,0,,They are all yours?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:25.67,0:47:27.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, absolutely. They're all legitimate.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:27.58,0:47:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Political affiliation?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:30.38,0:47:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía\Nmanaged to connect
Dialogue: 0,0:47:32.67,0:47:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,the wind-up ballerina\Nto the mechanism of the clock,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:36.67,0:47:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And the toy danced uninterruptedly
Dialogue: 0,0:47:38.54,0:47:41.62,Default,,0,0,0,,to the rhythm of its own music\Nfor three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:41.71,0:47:42.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:44.71,0:47:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been working for three days.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:47.42,0:47:49.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know what that means, son?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:50.58,0:47:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That discovery excited him
Dialogue: 0,0:47:52.33,0:47:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,more than any of\Nhis other madcap endeavors.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:55.92,0:47:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Without Ursula's supervision,\Nhe became lost in his own imagination.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:00.67,0:48:02.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Her skin became\Ncoarse like bark.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.42,0:48:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Her hair turned to leaves.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:06.13,0:48:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Poor Apollo.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.71,0:48:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Apollo ultimately understood\Nthat she'd never love him back
Dialogue: 0,0:48:10.54,0:48:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and that she'd never be his wife,\Nbut then he made her this promise.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.75,0:48:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That from that moment on,\Nshe would be his tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.63,0:48:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, Moscote.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:19.25,0:48:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,We have\Nno political affiliations here in Macondo.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:22.17,0:48:25.09,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't see the need for a census.\NWe all know each other here.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:25.17,0:48:26.80,Default,,0,0,0,,These are government orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:31.46,0:48:32.71,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:33.88,0:48:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.29,0:48:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen, that in-law of yours\Nis pushing it too far around here.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:40.79,0:48:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'm sorry, but the fact that one\Nof his daughters is marrying your son
Dialogue: 0,0:48:44.21,0:48:46.88,Default,,0,0,0,,doesn't give him the right\Nto do whatever he wants.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.96,0:48:48.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you should put a stop to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:53.42,0:48:54.42,Default,,0,0,0,,What's today?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:55.13,0:48:56.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Tuesday. Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:58.92,0:49:00.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I was thinking it might be.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.71,0:49:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's actually still Monday.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.21,0:49:43.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Úrsula's absence made\Nthe house seem enormous and empty.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.50,0:50:12.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Prudencio.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.33,0:50:15.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Prudencio Aguilar.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:17.33,0:50:19.00,Default,,0,0,0,,How did you end up so far away?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.92,0:50:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The need for company led me to find you.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.50,0:50:28.21,Default,,0,0,0,,My dear, sweet, old enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.46,0:50:31.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I was wondering where you were.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.25,0:50:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Macondo was\Nan unknown town to the dead
Dialogue: 0,0:50:40.38,0:50:42.13,Default,,0,0,0,,until its first dead man arrived.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:44.08,0:50:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:45.38,0:50:47.84,Default,,0,0,0,,He showed us a little black dot…
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.71,0:50:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,on the maps of death.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:41.08,0:51:42.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Papa…
Dialogue: 0,0:51:46.79,0:51:47.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama…
Dialogue: 0,0:51:52.08,0:51:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Papa…
Dialogue: 0,0:51:56.67,0:51:57.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Mama…
Dialogue: 0,0:51:58.54,0:52:00.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, Mr. Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.88,0:52:02.84,Default,,0,0,0,,-Is everything okay?\N-Papa…
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.04,0:52:07.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Prudencio…
Dialogue: 0,0:52:08.75,0:52:09.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades…
Dialogue: 0,0:52:11.50,0:52:14.08,Default,,0,0,0,,They are all so lonely in death.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:31.63,0:52:32.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What's today?
Dialogue: 0,0:52:33.46,0:52:35.54,Default,,0,0,0,,-Thursday.\N-Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.33,0:52:37.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It still is Monday.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:39.00,0:52:41.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The time traveling machine\Nhas broken down,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.00,0:52:45.29,Default,,0,0,0,,and Úrsula and Amaranta are so far away.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:10.33,0:53:13.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Ya! Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:13.17,0:53:14.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:17.38,0:53:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:19.17,0:53:22.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Time has stopped,\Nand eternity has begun!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.33,0:53:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Ugh! Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:24.17,0:53:26.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-But man wasn't born…\N-Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:26.75,0:53:28.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.42,0:53:36.75,Default,,0,0,0,,-Ah!\N-Oh!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:36.83,0:53:40.12,Default,,0,0,0,,-We were born to die!\N-Ah! What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.21,0:53:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Call the neighbors!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:41.50,0:53:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Help! Somebody help!\N-To become…
Dialogue: 0,0:53:47.13,0:53:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,To become… organic matter!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:50.29,0:53:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Buendía!\NStay calm--
Dialogue: 0,0:53:54.50,0:53:55.71,Default,,0,0,0,,No more!
Dialogue: 0,0:54:37.21,0:54:39.96,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll be all right. Easy. Easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:40.04,0:54:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Easy. It's all right. It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:43.04,0:54:45.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Easy. Easy. Easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:46.08,0:54:48.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right. Calm down.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.04,0:56:22.04,Default,,0,0,0,,We were born to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.33,0:56:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,To become…
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.29,0:57:19.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And eternity has begun.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:23.54,0:57:26.75,Default,,0,0,0,,But man was not born to be eternal.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:28.71,0:57:31.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We were born to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:33.75,0:57:35.88,Default,,0,0,0,,To become organic matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:37.54,0:57:42.04,Default,,0,0,0,,To become memories\Nand oblivion in the hearts of men.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:37.79,0:59:40.08,Default,,0,0,0,,BASED ON THE NOVEL\NBY GABRIEL GARCÍA MÁRQUEZ
